     * [\p{L}\p{M}\p{N}] as PCRE2 10.35 (PHP 7.4) matches them. PCRE2 >= 10.40 (PHP 8.x) matches scripts by their script
     * extensions (CJK punctuation such as U+3001 joined a Han run) and knows newer Unicode letters, so the \p{} form gave
     * other documents on PHP 8.5 than on 7.4 (found by lane S acceptance 4 on PHP 7.4). Fixed sets = same bytes everywhere.
